{
  "_README": [
    "One representative map point per subsystem, for the DEMO dashboard.",
    "Derived, not surveyed: the MEDIAN position of the subsystem's own",
    "SOURCE and CORE members that have a coordinate in",
    "samples/gi_coordinates.json. Regenerate alongside that file.",
    "",
    "Why a derived centre and not one named GI: every subsystem has SEVERAL",
    "sources, and GITETs are shared between subsystems (GITET_NBRJA belongs",
    "to both SS_LBK and SS_BLL), so no single GITET can represent one.",
    "",
    "Why the median and not the mean: a subsystem often reaches one remote",
    "member whose coordinate would pull an average well away from the",
    "cluster where the subsystem actually sits.",
    "",
    "Why SOURCE and CORE only: SOURCE_BOUNDARY / EXTERNAL_CONTEXT / BOUNDARY",
    "members belong to a neighbouring subsystem or another UP2B, so counting",
    "them would place the dot outside this subsystem's own territory.",
    "",
    "'anchor_points' is how many DISTINCT coordinates the median is taken",
    "over, and 'members_with_coords' of 'members_total' how much of the",
    "subsystem is positioned at all. A LOW ratio means the dot rests on a",
    "small, possibly unrepresentative sample - treat it as 'this area',",
    "never as a site. Subsystems can also sit very close together (SS_GUCL",
    "and SS_SLCG resolve to the same point), so any map must spread",
    "overlapping markers rather than draw them raw.",
    "Inherits every caveat in samples/gi_coordinates.json."
  ],
